title "Basic Diagram Crawl/Walk Maturity"
# not modelled: App/Software/Hardware Product models, Vendor and SLA tags, domain legend, explanatory notes

BA app-a: Application A
BA app-b: Application B
BA app-c: Application C SaaS

SI app-a-prod: App A PROD
SI app-b-prod: App B PROD
SI app-c-prod: App C SaaS Prod

TMSO app-a-support: App A Support
TMSO app-b-support: App B Support
TMSO windows-admin: Windows Administration
TMSO sql-support: SQL Support
TMSO network-support: Network Support

TMS app-mgmt: App Mgmt Services
TMS compute: Compute/ Hosting
TMS database: Database Services
TMS network: Network Services

DCG win-servers: All Win Servers
DCG mssql-apps: MSSQL Apps
DCG network-gear: Network Gear

CI(Application) appa-ci: AppA@server123
CI(Application) appb-ci: AppB@server456
CI(Windows Server) server123: Server123
CI(Windows Server) server456: Server456
CI(Database) mssql123: MSSQL@server123
CI(Database) mssql456: MSSQL@server456
CI(Switch) switch1001: Switch1001
CI(Router) router01: Router 01

app-a -> app-a-prod
app-b -> app-b-prod
app-c -> app-c-prod

# The App A Support "Contains" connector is attached to App C SaaS Prod; it runs behind
# App A PROD and App B PROD (no arrowhead at either). Likely meant App A PROD, but the
# slide links App A Support only to App C SaaS Prod; App A PROD has no Contains.
# deck vectors: this Contains connector is attached to App C SaaS Prod but runs
# exactly along the centre line behind App A PROD (no other tech offering contains
# it) and App B PROD (contained by App B Support). Slide 16 attaches the same
# connector (same shape id) to App A PROD. Read: contains App A PROD, and App C as drawn.
app-a-support -> app-a-prod
app-a-support -> app-c-prod
app-b-support -> app-b-prod
app-a-support -> app-mgmt
app-b-support -> app-mgmt

windows-admin -> win-servers
windows-admin -> compute
sql-support -> mssql-apps
sql-support -> database
network-support -> network-gear
network-support -> network

win-servers -> server123
win-servers -> server456
mssql-apps -> mssql123
mssql-apps -> mssql456
network-gear -> switch1001
network-gear -> router01

# service mapping (blue)
app-a-prod -> appa-ci
app-b-prod -> appb-ci
appa-ci -> server123 : Runs On
appb-ci -> server456 : Runs On
server123 -> mssql123
# Server456 -> MSSQL@server456 passes behind MSSQL@server123 (arrowhead only at MSSQL@server456)
server456 -> mssql456
# a single connector MSSQL@server456 -> Router 01 passes behind Switch1001, so it looks
# like a MSSQL -> Switch -> Router chain; Switch1001 has no blue link of its own
# deck vectors: this connector is attached to Router 01 but runs exactly along the
# centre line behind Switch1001, which has no mapping of its own -> read as a chain
mssql456 -> switch1001
switch1001 -> router01
